    "answer": "kombu-(usu.-Saccharina-japonica)/konbu/kelp/any-edible-species-from-the-family-Laminariaceae",
    "mnemonic": "<kanji>Insect</kanji> <kanji>cloth</kanji> is actually <vocabulary>konbu</vocabulary>. <vocabulary>Konbu seaweed</vocabulary> is very common in Japan, and it's delicious. And insects happen to love using it as cloth, too. They make all their clothes out of konbu.",
